== write: conversions
ok integer: text that is no number
ok integer: text out of range
ok integer: negative text
ok integer: an integral float
ok integer: a float out of range
ok integer: the lowest value as LargeInt
ok integer: one above the highest value
ok a failed write leaves the value
ok largeint: text that is no number
ok largeint: an integral float
ok largeint: a fraction
ok largeint: a float out of range
ok float: text that is no number
ok float: exponent text
ok boolean: FALSE
ok boolean: 1
ok boolean: other text
ok boolean: 0
ok boolean: any other number is True
ok datetime: text that is no date
ok datetime: a float
ok date: text that is no date
ok date: a float loses its time part
ok date: a negative value is truncated towards zero
ok time: text that is no time
ok time: a float loses its date part
ok time: the time of day of a negative value
ok string: a float is stored as text
ok string: the empty string is a value
ok not null
== write: size
ok a value of exactly Size characters
ok one character more
ok a converted value that is too long
ok the value is unchanged
ok no limit when Size is 0
ok no limit for a memo
== write: state
ok a setter in dsBrowse
ok Clear in dsBrowse
ok Text := in dsBrowse
ok Text := '' in dsBrowse
ok the value is unchanged
== write: read-only fields
ok CanModify of a plain field
ok CanModify of a read-only field
ok an auto-increment field is read-only by default
ok so it cannot be modified
ok CanModify of a column the driver cannot update
ok writing a read-only field
ok clearing a read-only field
ok Text := on a read-only field
ok writing the auto-increment field
ok the read-only check comes before the conversion
ok writing a column the driver cannot update
ok nothing was modified
ok the state check comes first
ok OnNewRecord may assign a read-only field
ok and another one
ok after the event the field is read-only again
ok no field of a read-only dataset can be modified
== write: closed dataset
ok a setter on a closed dataset
ok Clear on a closed dataset
ok CanModify on a closed dataset
ok a setter without a dataset
ok CanModify without a dataset
== write: assignment sequence
ok OnValidate, OnChange, notification
ok Modified
ok an equal value runs the whole sequence
ok a conversion error
ok happens before OnValidate
ok and leaves the value
ok Clear runs the sequence
ok and sets null
ok Text := runs the sequence
ok only the written field is flagged
== write: OnValidate rejects
ok the exception of OnValidate propagates
ok neither OnChange nor a notification
ok the previous value is restored
ok Modified is restored
ok and so is the flag
ok a rejected second write restores the first one
ok still Modified
ok still flagged
